#: ../../circom.md:50
msgid "Step 2: Generate the R1CS file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../circom.md:52
msgid "Your compiled circuit needs to be translated into a form the proving system can reason about mathematically. That form is the R1CS file. The proving system uses the R1CS file to check that a witness (your execution trace, generated in the next step) actually satisfies all the rules of the circuit. Without it, there is nothing to verify against."
msgstr ""

#: ../../circom.md:54
msgid "This is also the point where you choose a **proving scheme**. The proving scheme defines the mathematics used to construct and verify your proof. The R1CS file itself is scheme-agnostic, but the cryptographic keys generated from it in a later stage will be tied to whichever scheme you choose here. This tutorial uses **Groth16**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../circom.md:56
msgid "To generate the R1CS file tied to the Groth16 scheme, run the `scripts/groth16/groth16_trusted_setup.ts` script. Similarly, to tie the R1CS file to the Plonk scheme, run the `scripts/plonk/plonk_trusted_setup.ts` script."
msgstr ""

